//==
// # Elements by arity, and the two diagonal splits of a quad (v1-types, chunk T1)
//
// UvTriangulation and FaceMesh number their elements triangles first, then quads, in one
// ElementIndex, and ElementCorners returns an Array<VertexIndex> whose Count says which kind it
// was. Every reader then re-derives the arity (`ps.Count == 3 ? ... : ps[3]`) and reads corners by
// position. Three readers measure a quad against the surface, each its own way:
//   - F1's grid keep rule (GridElementWithinChordal, FlatDistanceOf, deleted at T1's merge):
//     the nearer of the two triangles on the diagonal from corner 0;
//   - the library's deviation measures (ElementCoverageGap, FlatElementDistance): the same;
//   - the version 1 gate (QuadSplitsWithin): each of the four triangles of both diagonal splits.
// The contract (README, "Version 1 mesh contract") is the third: a quad is within the chordal
// bound only if both of its diagonal splits are, so a renderer may split it either way.
// ElementShape keeps the arity in the type, and QuadSplits names the four triangles once, so the
// keep rule and the gate read one definition.
//
// Sections, in order:
//  - Elements by arity
//  - Diagonal splits
//  - Grid decisions

//==
// # Elements by arity

// One element of a triangulation or a face mesh, by its corners in winding order.
//   TriangleShape: element k < Triangles.Count.
//   QuadShape: element k at or past Triangles.Count, below ElementCount.
//   NoElement: k is out of range, a case of its own instead of an index error.
type ElementShape
    implements IValue
    = TriangleShape(Face: TriangleFace)
    | QuadShape(Face: QuadFace)
    | NoElement(Index: ElementIndex);

//==
// # Diagonal splits

// One split of a quad on a diagonal into two triangles, each keeping the quad's winding.
type QuadSplit
    implements IValue
{
    First: TriangleFace;
    Second: TriangleFace;
}

// Both diagonal splits of a quad (A B C D): on the diagonal A C, (A B C) and (A C D); on the
// diagonal B D, (B C D) and (B D A). The contract's chordal and orientation claims on a quad
// hold when they hold on all four triangles.
type QuadSplits
    implements IValue
{
    OnAC: QuadSplit;
    OnBD: QuadSplit;
}

//==
// # Grid decisions

// Whether a quad grid is within the chordal bound, with the evidence.
//   GridWithinChordal: every triangle an element renders as (RenderTriangles: a triangle, or
//     both splits of a quad) is within Bound of the surface at refinement's samples, and no
//     element folds when lifted. Built only by DecideGridChordal.
//   GridExceedsAt: Element is the first element that folds or strays; the face takes the
//     refined triangulation.
type GridChordalDecision
    implements IValue
    = GridWithinChordal(Grid: UvTriangulation, Bound: Number)
    | GridExceedsAt(Element: ElementIndex);
